Dialogue: 0,0:35:10.74,0:35:15.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,GPU dominates nearly 7:1 GPU heavy.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:15.48,0:35:19.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,In contrast, let's take a look at an agentic AI system.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.80,0:35:22.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Across the top, look at the pipeline stages.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:22.20,0:35:25.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Green is GPU work, blue is CPU work.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:25.88,0:35:31.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Linting is happening on our Xeon 6 plus processor with efficient efficiency cores.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:31.76,0:35:37.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Web fetch and compile is happening on our Xeon 6 performance cores.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:37.40,0:35:44.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And unit testing is coming back and running on our Xeon 6 plus efficient efficiency cores.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:44.16,0:35:47.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,The right class CPU for each stage of the pipeline.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:47.48,0:35:49.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Take a look at the slider across the top again.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:49.88,0:35:54.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're near parity, but CPU heavy this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.64,0:36:01.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's this look like when we multiply that by millions of queries a day?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:01.24,0:36:06.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,As you mentioned, each Xeon 6 plus processor has up to 288 cores.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:06.27,0:36:12.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's 576 cores per two socket server.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:12.08,0:36:21.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,When we look at that from a rack scale perspective, that gives us over 36,000 cores per 32 use of compute space.
