Dialogue: 0,0:45:58.12,0:46:04.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,They both get the fed the same prompt and the same model just different stacks.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:04.40,0:46:07.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,The disaggregated inference stack is taking off.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:07.68,0:46:15.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what's happening here is you have the Xeon 6 processors doing all the tooling execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:15.20,0:46:20.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have Sambanova RDUs doing the decode and generating all of the tokens.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:20.45,0:46:29.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then you got the GPUs performing the prompt caching and the faster prefill reducing overall time.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:29.08,0:46:39.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,When all three chips are working together, you dramatically reduce the end-to-end latency and the agents for the fastest need for intelligent AI.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:39.88,0:46:45.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,On the other side, the GPU stack is still working away.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:45.80,0:46:55.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the initial results of our work is disaggregated inference is the and the GPUs, the RDUs, the CPUs, that's the fastest.
